{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e4be16c5c888c503","name":"Vehicle Attacks","source":{"id":"source:reference-e4be16c5c888c503","title":"Vehicle Attacks","revision":27390,"timestamp":"2026-03-02T22:46:11Z","sha256":"5d939396b81f78efdc27c092b550dc3d152120009ae360778dc519347b1c762b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=27390","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Vehicle%20Attacks&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e4be16c5c888c503","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Any Vehicle equipped with weapons can make attacks against opponents within ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," Weapon Range (see below). An attack roll with a Vehicle Weapon is calculated as follows:\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Vehicle Attack: 1d20 + ",{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"}," + Vehicle's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," Modifier + Weapon Range Modifier"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"},":"]}," Use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"}," of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," (which, in some cases, may be the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"},").\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["If you are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained"}," in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," skill, you gain a +2 bonus on all attacks made with any Vehicle Weapon identified as being crewed by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"},"."]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," Modifier:"]}," A Vehicle's computer improves the accuracy of the Vehicle's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"},", and the Vehicle's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," score measures the quality of the computer."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Weapon Range Modifier:"]}," A Vehicle Weapon can attack a target at Point-Blank, Short, Medium, or Long Range.\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["If you make a Vehicle Attack against a target within Point-Blank Range, you take no penalty on the attack roll; your penalty on attack rolls increases to\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["-2 at Short Range,"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["-5 at Medium Range,"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["and -10 at Long Range."]}]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Critical Hits:"]}," When you roll a Natural 20 on your attack, you automatically hit the target and deal double damage. When using a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Weapon"},", you cannot apply any effect that causes an automatic Natural 20 or automatic ",{"tag":"a","children":["Critical Hit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Critical_Hit"}," (such as spending a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Destiny Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Destiny_Point"}," or using the Jedi Master’s ",{"tag":"a","children":["Serenity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Serenity"}," class feature), unless a rule specifies that it can be used with Vehicle Attacks."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Automatic Misses:"]}," If you roll a Natural 1 on your attack, you automatically miss."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Vehicle Damage: (Weapon Damage + 1/2 Pilot's Heroic Level + Miscellaneous Modifiers) x Damage Multiplier"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Damage Multiplier:"]}," After rolling the weapon damage dice, multiply the result by the listed Damage Multiplier. For example, when you fire a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Weapon"}," that deals 6d10x2 damage, roll 6d10 and multiply the result by 2."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Mass Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Individual ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mass Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mass_Combat"}," can make attacks against ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"}," as normal. Vehicle Battalions follow all the same restrictions as Nonvehicle Battalions on their attacks. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," and Vehicle ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"}," use the standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"}," for determining the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"}," on their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"},". ",{"tag":"a","children":["Character Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Character_Scale"}," weapons, such as those wielded by Nonvehicle Battalions, use the table for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ranged Attacks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ranged_Attacks","referenceId":"reference:3c89b302f9fd687b"}," to determine their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"}," at ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["All normal weapon ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"}," penalties still apply.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Orbital Bombardment"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Combatants in a ground battle can be devastated by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," in orbit above the planet. As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},", the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Commander"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Commander","referenceId":"reference:16af7be312e1840b"}," of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," can order a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon System"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_System"}," to aim at  single square on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mass Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mass_Combat"}," battlefield. The square is considered to be at Long ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"}," for the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},", and the ship must make an attack roll against a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of 10 to hit the target square. If successful, all ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"}," in that square take normal damage for that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon System"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_System"},", or half damage on a miss. That ship cannot make any other attacks until the beginning of the Commander's next turn.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Orbital Bombardment should be used by the Gamemaster only as a means of making a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mass Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mass_Combat"}," encounter more dangerous. A single shot from a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," weapon is usually more than enough to destroy a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"},", so Orbital Bombardment should not be used lightly. Orbital Bombardment should occur only if the needs of the adventure require it rather than as a means for resolving combat.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Falling Vehicles"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["When a flying ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Battalion","referenceId":"reference:95b230a4151c488b"}," is ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disabled"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disabled"}," (but not destroyed) in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mass Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mass_Combat"},", the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," falls to the ground and might damage ground ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"},". At the beginning of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disabled"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disabled"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Uncontrolled"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Uncontrolled"}," flying Vehicle's turn, that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," crashes into the ground in the square it occupies. All nonflying ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"}," in that square take damage equal to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Collision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Collision"}," damage for a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," of that size.\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunners"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunners"}," (including the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Copilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Copilot","referenceId":"reference:49f5b0e488cfa66c"},", if there are Pilot-operated weapons on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},") can make an attack with their Vehicle Weapon as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},". The maximum Range and the Range Modifiers of a Vehicle Attack depend on the Vehicle Weapon used (see below). Capital Ship Weapons are designed for long-range bombardment against large or immobile targets, and they have difficulty tracking very small targets. When attacking a target of less than Colossal size, a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," that is Colossal (Frigate) size or larger takes a -20 penalty on its attack rolls. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Point-Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Point-Defense"}," weapons are specifically designed to attack smaller targets, and do not take these penalties.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Just as in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Character Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Character_Scale"}," combat, vehicle facing and fire arcs are not used . It's assumed that the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," is orienting the ship in the most advantageous way possible during combat, and most ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," in the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Star Wars"]}," universe are quite maneuverable in any event.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"caption","children":["Vehicle Weapon Ranges\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WEAPON TYPE\n"],"rowspan":2},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["RANGE BY CHARACTER SCALE\n"],"colspan":4},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["\n"],"rowspan":11},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["RANGE BY STARSHIP SCALE\n"],"colspan":4}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["POINT-BLANK\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SHORT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MEDIUM\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["LONG\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["POINT-BLANK\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SHORT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MEDIUM\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["LONG\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Cannons"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-120 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["121-240 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["241-600 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["601-1,200 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-1 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["3-4 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5-8 Squares\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Cannons"},"**\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-300 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["301-600 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["601-1,500 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1,501-3,000 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-2 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["3-4 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5-10 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["11-20 Squares\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-150 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["151-300 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["301-750 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["751-1,500 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-1 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["3-5 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["6-10 Squares\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Point-Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Point-Defense"},"*\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-150 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["151-300 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["301-750 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["751-1,500 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-1 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["3-5 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["6-10 Squares\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Turbolasers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Turbolasers"},"*\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-600 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["601-1,200 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1,201-3,000 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["3,001-6,000 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-4 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5-8 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["9-20 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["21-40 Squares\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Missiles or Torpedoes\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-450 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["451-900 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["901-2,250 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2,251-4,500 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-3 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["4-6 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["7-15 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["16-30 Squares\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Tractor Beams"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tractor_Beams"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-150 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["151-300 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["301-750 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["751-1,500 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-1 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["3-5 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["6-10 Squares\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Gravity Well Projectors"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gravity_Well_Projectors"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-1,500 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-10 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Shieldbuster Torpedoes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shieldbuster_Torpedoes","referenceId":"reference:a040cdc2053302dc"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-450 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["451-900 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["901-2,250 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2,251-4,000 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-3 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["4-6 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["7-15 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["16-30 Squares\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["*This ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon System"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_System"}," can only be mounted on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," of Colossal (Frigate) size or larger."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["**Heavy and Hapan Triple variants can only be mounted on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," of Colossal (Frigate) size or larger; this restriction doesn't apply to Light and Medium variants."]},"\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Missiles and Torpedoes"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Some Vehicles carry guided projectile weapons such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Proton Torpedoes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Proton_Torpedoes","referenceId":"reference:89c41c332c03f2dd"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concussion Missiles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concussion_Missiles","referenceId":"reference:c95ee0f6eb24f16e"},". Attacks with these weapons are resolved just as with any other weapon. If you ",{"tag":"a","children":["Aim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Aim","referenceId":"reference:28427fa78a230e42"}," before making an attack with a Missile or Torpedo, it locks on to the target, and can track its target independently. Make your attack roll normally, but if you miss, the Missile or Torpedo can attempt to attack again on your next turn. This next attack is made using the same attack bonus, but with a -5 penalty. (You do not need to spend an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Action"}," to make this attack.) If the Missile or Torpedo misses its target a second time, it self-destructs harmlessly.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Attacking a Missile or Torpedo"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["If a Missile or Torpedo misses its target initially, it is possible to shoot it down before it attacks again. A Missile or Torpedo has a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of 30, 10 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},", and it is considered to occupy the same square as its target for purposes of determining ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"}," penalties. It is also possible to attack a Missile or Torpedo prior to its first attack, but you must have ",{"tag":"a","children":["Readied an Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Readied_an_Action"}," specifically for this purpose.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Weapon Batteries"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A Weapon Battery is a cluster of up to six identical weapons. If a Starship has Weapon Batteries, special rules apply when a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," Aids Another ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," in the same Weapon Battery.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["First, the Aiding ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," automatically gains a +2 bonus on the attack roll; no attack roll is required to determine whether the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Aid Another"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Aid_Another","referenceId":"reference:276932074aab1852"}," attempt is successful. Second, for every three points by which the attack roll exceeds the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},", the target is hit by another weapon in the Battery, adding +1 die to the weapon's damage. (Apply this extra damage before applying the weapon's damage multiplier, if any.) If a Starship has Weapon Batteries, its statistics include the modified attack bonus because these weapons are usually fired as a group. However, the weapons may still fire independently without the bonus, if you wish.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In addition, a Weapon Battery can also ",{"tag":"a","children":["Aid Another"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Aid_Another","referenceId":"reference:276932074aab1852"}," Weapon Battery. In this case, only one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," in the Aiding Battery needs to make an attack roll against a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of 10. If successful, add a +2 bonus on the attack roll for every weapon in the Aided Battery. Unlike weapons in the same Battery, there is no chance that these extra weapons hit the target, regardless of how much the attack roll exceeds the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," should use Weapon Batteries to keep things moving along- no one wants to make attack rolls for the dozens of weapons on a Star Destroyer. There are two ways you can use Weapon Batteries:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Narrow Salvo"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["This method, the default use of a Weapon Battery (as described above), is ideal for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," that are attacking other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Stations"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Stations","referenceId":"reference:65763f09c9074f45"}," because it brackets the target while concentrating fire, dealing significant damage to targets that have a high ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Proximity Spread"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Instead of trying to land multiple hits, a Weapon Battery can spread its fire in a way that maximizes the chance that one will hit (ideal for attacking ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},"). A Proximity Spread is resolved as an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Area Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area_Attack"},", but it affects only 1 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"}," square on the battle grid. As with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Autofire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Autofire"},", the Weapon Battery takes a -5 penalty on its attack roll.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Tactical Fire"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A number of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," have a Tactical Fire option, an alternative ability that allows them to function more like commanders than like individual ships. Each Tactical Fire option produces an \"aura\" around the ship that affects the battlefield, replacing all of the Capital Ship's normal attacks in a given round. When engaged in combat against other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},", a Capital Ship is better off using its normal attacks because they have the greatest chance of dealing the most damage.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Tactical Fire option is provided as a means of using Capital-scale ships in space combat scenarios without making them another enemy that the heroes need to defeat. In essence, using the Tactical Fire option transforms a Capital Ship from an opponent into an obstacle or complication. This should allow you to include ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," in a combat scenario, adding an interesting element to the fight without the danger of blowing the heroes out of the sky with a lucky shot.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Focused Fire"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["All ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," have the ability to focus their weapons on a large area of space, allowing the vessel to make a Starship Scale ",{"tag":"a","children":["Area Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area_Attack"},". Essentially, Focused Fire creates dangerous \"terrain\" in space by filling large areas of the battlefield with a hail of weapons fire. Much like the Tactical Fire option (see above), this allows Gamemasters to use ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," in a new way without making the ship into a direct combatant. A Colossal (Frigate) size ship can attack a single square with Focused Fire, a Colossal (Cruiser) size ship can attack a 2x2-square area, and a Colossal (Station) ship can attack a 3x3-square area.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," selects a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannon","referenceId":"reference:0911ab4bc0e93386"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Turbolaser"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Turbolaser","referenceId":"reference:3f6c338dc202fcde"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Cannon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Cannon","referenceId":"reference:815dc6c626750487"}," system as its primary source of Focused Fire. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," must forgo all other attacks in the round it uses Focused Fire, making an attack roll against a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of 10 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"}," penalties apply). If successful, that area is targeted by Focused Fire. If a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," ends its turn in an area targeted by Focused Fire, compare the result of the attack roll to the Starship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},". If the attack roll is higher, the target takes normal damage from the chosen ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon System"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_System"},"; if the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," is higher, the target takes half damage.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
